---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { KINDS } from '../lib/collections';
import { SITE_NAME, PUBLISHER, abs, rel } from '../lib/site';

const counts: Record<string, number> = {};
for (const k of KINDS) counts[k] = (await getCollection(k)).length;
const total = Object.values(counts).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);
const repo = 'https://github.com/Jairaj1234-dancer/nighantu';
const year = 2026;
---
<Page
  title="Cite the Nighantu"
  description="How to cite the Age Ayurveda Nighantu, what licence applies, and what the work is derived from."
  canonical="/cite/"
  lede="How to cite this work, and what you are allowed to do with it."
>

## Citing a single page

Every monograph carries its own citation at the foot, with the canonical URL and the
date that page was last revised. Use that in preference to a site-level citation, because
page revision dates differ and only the page knows its own.

## Citing the work as a whole

<p><strong>Plain:</strong></p>

<p>{PUBLISHER}. <i>{SITE_NAME}</i>. {year}. <a href={abs('/')}>{abs('/')}</a></p>

<p><strong>BibTeX:</strong></p>

<pre><code>{`@misc{ageayurveda_nighantu_${year},
  author       = {{${PUBLISHER}}},
  title        = {{${SITE_NAME}: a referenced encyclopedia of Ayurvedic materia medica}},
  year         = {${year}},
  howpublished = {\\url{${abs('/')}}},
  note         = {${total} monographs. Content CC BY 4.0.}
}`}</code></pre>

<p>
  Machine-readable metadata is in <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/CITATION.cff`}>CITATION.cff</a>,
  so GitHub's "Cite this repository" button works directly.
</p>

## Licence

<table class="facts">
  <caption>What applies where</caption>
  <tbody>
    <tr><th scope="row">Reference content</th><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Scripts and site code</th><td>MIT</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Brand, product names, product photography</th><td>Not licensed</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<p>
  Attribute to {PUBLISHER}, {SITE_NAME}, with a link to the page you used.
</p>

## What this is derived from

The monographs are not original prose. They restructure and extend material from the
Amidha Ayurveda Herb Database, used under CC BY 4.0, with classical citations and
editorial layers added by us. That upstream credit travels with any redistribution.

The full statement, including what we deliberately do not publish and where the work is
weakest, is in <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/PROVENANCE.md`}>PROVENANCE.md</a>. It is worth
reading before citing: it records that no practitioner has reviewed the monographs line
by line, so this must not be cited as clinically reviewed.

## For automated readers

<p>
  Every page has a plain-Markdown twin at its URL with <code>.md</code> appended. There is a
  curated index at <a href={rel('/llms.txt')}>llms.txt</a> and a full-text index at
  <a href={rel('/llms-full.txt')}>llms-full.txt</a>. Quote and cite freely; a link back is
  the whole of what the licence asks.
</p>
</Page>
